<title>AUSTRALIA: AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - May 16.</title>
<headline>AWB Australia wheat indicator prices - May 16.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-05-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian Wheat Board international card prices for wheat exports for May 16.</p>
<p>In U.S. dollars per tonne, FOB eastern states.</p>
<p>		ASW	  AH     PH 13 PCT  PH 14 PCT</p>
<p>    May    212.00    215.50    216.00     220.00</p>
<p>    Jun    208.00    211.50    212.00     219.00</p>
<p>    Jul    205.00    208.50    209.00     218.00</p>
<p>    Aug    202.50    206.00    206.50     216.00</p>
<p>    Sept   202.50    206.00    206.50     216.00</p>
<p>    Oct    203.50    207.00    207.50     217.00</p>
<p>    Geelong	 160.50	     Esperance	    165.75</p>
<p>    Portland	161.50	     Albany		 166.75</p>
<p>					     Fremantle	    168.75</p>
<p>					     Geraldton	    166.75</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract fob price quoted on a delivered port basis, offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1997/98 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (0630 GMT).</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
